/**
 * @file ggsw_ciphertext.dox
 * @brief Documentation of the GGSW ciphertext representation.
 *
 * This file contains the documentation of the GGSW
 * ciphertext encoding used in the library. It is intended for
 * understanding the mathematical structure rather than the API.
 */

/**
 * @page ggsw_ciphertext GGSW Ciphertext
 *
 * @section ggsw_overview Overview
 *
 * A GGSW ciphertext encodes a small integer polynomial represented
 * by a function @p f.
 *
 * The ciphertext is represented as a matrix of size
 * @p n_limbs_tilde × @p n_limbs with coefficients in ℤₙ[X].
 *
 * Each row @p i is a GLWE ciphertext encrypting @p f(H(i)).
 *
 * @verbatim
 * [
 *   GLWE(f(H(0)))
 *   ...
 *   GLWE(f(H(n_limbs_tilde - 1)))
 * ]
 * @endverbatim
 *
 * @section ggsw_gadget Gadget matrix
 *
 * The gadget matrix @p H is built using the gadget base
 * @p bg = 2^{kappa_tilde}.
 *
 * It is reorganized in powers of @p bg in order to preserve
 * the prefix property.
 *
 * @verbatim
 * [ 1/bg        0         0    ...     0 ]
 * [ 0        1/bg         0    ...     0 ]
 * [ ...        ...        ...           ]
 * [ 0           0         0    ...  1/bg ]
 *
 * [ 1/bg^2      0         0    ...     0 ]
 * [ 0        1/bg^2       0    ...     0 ]
 * [ ...        ...        ...           ]
 * [ 0           0         0    ...  1/bg^2 ]
 *
 * ...
 *
 * [ 1/bg^{l_t}  0         0    ...     0 ]
 * [ ...        ...        ...           ]
 * [ 0           0         0    ...  1/bg^{l_t} ]
 * @endverbatim
 *
 * Each block corresponds to one power of the gadget base.
 *
 * @section ggsw_partial Partial GGSW ciphertext
 *
 * A partial GGSW ciphertext (denoted @p partialGGSW) is obtained by
 * restricting the full GGSW ciphertext to a subset of rows corresponding
 * to a fixed power of the gadget base @p Bg.
 *
 * More precisely, for a given gadget level @p j, the partial GGSW is the
 * submatrix of the GGSW ciphertext that encrypts the polynomial
 * @p f multiplied by the gadget vector entries associated with
 * @p 1 / Bg^{j}.
 *
 * In terms of the gadget matrix @p H, a partial GGSW corresponds to one
 * block of @p n_limbs consecutive rows:
 *
 * @verbatim
 * [ 1/Bg^{j}      0           0      ...     0 ]
 * [ 0         1/Bg^{j}        0      ...     0 ]
 * [ ...           ...        ...             ]
 * [ 0             0           0      ...  1/Bg^{j} ]
 * @endverbatim
 *
 * Each row of this block is a GLWE ciphertext encrypting
 * @p f multiplied by the corresponding gadget coefficient.
 *
 * A full GGSW ciphertext can thus be seen as the vertical concatenation
 * of all partial GGSW ciphertexts for @p j = 1, ..., l_tilde.
 */

